              </span></span></span><![endif]><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span
              style='font-size:11.5pt;font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
              color:#414141;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB'>Monitor</span></b><span
              style='font-size:11.5pt;font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
              color:#414141;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB'>. Following Certification, based on
              information collected through your Submission concerning the technologies used
              by the firm and your history, the Bank may from time to time post information
              to the Service, including information which articulates technology changes
              (such as software patches or updates) or external security threats (such as
              malicious code or viruses) that may be relevant to, or concern, the firm.<span
              style="mso-spacerun:yes">&nbsp; </span>You agree to regularly monitor the
              Service for, and review, such posted materials. We may communicate with you in
              regard to such information to inquire as to what steps the firm has taken as a
              consequence of such information that the Bank has shared through the Service or
              otherwise. If the Bank requests additional information from you, including in
              relation to how the firm has responded to identified security threats or
              similar issues, you agree to provide any such requested information that is
              reasonably sufficient to satisfy the Bank that the identified security threats
              or issues have been addressed so as to not present a continued risk to the
              Bank. The Bank strongly encourages the firm to regularly update the technology
              and history portions of the Service from time to time so as to keep the Bank
              reasonably appraised of those incidents, changes and updates to the firmÕs
              information security environment and practices which may reasonably impact or
              affect the Bank. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

