              <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:
              inter-ideograph;line-height:15.6pt;background:white'><span
              style='font-size:11.5pt;font-family:Arial;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
              color:#414141;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB'>(b)<span style='mso-tab-count:1'> </span>The
              Bank maintains an information security program which implements reasonable and
              appropriate physical, organizational and technological measures designed to
              secure data against unauthorized access (<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Bank
              Security Measures</b>). The Bank will deploy the Bank Security Measures to
              protect Firm Data while under its control. Without limiting the foregoing, all
              Firm Data submitted to the Service is automatically encrypted using 128</span><span
              style='font-size:11.5pt;font-family:"Cambria Math";mso-fareast-font-family:
              "Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:"Cambria Math";color:#414141;mso-ansi-language:
              EN-GB'>&#8208;</span><span style='font-size:11.5pt;font-family:Arial;
              mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";color:#414141;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB'>bit
              security. Information which maps the identity of the firm to the Service
              identification credentials provided to the firm is kept confidential offline
              and outside of the Service systems. The Bank is the only person with the key to
              decrypt the Firm Data. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

              <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:
